        // [LOCAL-PATCH] Injected by idac-localstack/publishers/transformation-engine/
        // patches/GlueClientProvider.scala.local-glue-endpoint.payload — applied
        // transiently for builds that target the local stack and reverted right
        // after sbt assembly (see apply-local-build-patches.sh / revert-local-build-patches.sh).
        //
        // Rationale: the upstream non-local branch builds the Glue SDK client
        // with no explicit endpoint or region, which means it talks to real
        // glue.<region>.amazonaws.com and 400s with UnrecognizedClientException
        // for our test/test creds. The upstream "local" branch is gated on a
        // FILE_SYSTEM=local env var that nothing in this stack sets, and it
        // hard-codes http://localhost:9999 as the mock endpoint anyway — which
        // doesn't match LocalStack at http://localstack:4566. Rather than
        // wiring FILE_SYSTEM and a separate mock, we honour AWS_ENDPOINT_URL
        // (the same env var S3A and the rest of the SDK look at). When it's
        // unset (real QA/prod) this branch is dead code and behaviour is
        // identical to the upstream one-liner.
        sys.env.get("AWS_ENDPOINT_URL") match {
          case Some(endpoint) =>
            AWSGlueClientBuilder
              .standard()
              .withEndpointConfiguration(new AwsClientBuilder.EndpointConfiguration(
                endpoint,
                sys.env.getOrElse("AWS_REGION", sys.env.getOrElse("AWS_DEFAULT_REGION", region))))
              .withCredentials(new AWSStaticCredentialsProvider(new BasicAWSCredentials(accessKey, secretKey)))
              .build()
          case None =>
            AWSGlueClientBuilder.standard().build()
        }
